{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01WRkcaCFThyS84hCpxNKh7q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see that:\n\n1. In `layout.tsx`, the `alternates.types` metadata already includes `\"application/rss+xml\"` and `\"application/feed+json\"`, which maps to Next.js's `<link rel=\"alternate\">` tags. However, the story requires explicit `<link>` tags in the HTML head.\n\nLooking more carefully at `layout.tsx`:\n- Line 59-61: `alternates.types` already has `\"application/rss+xml\"` and `\"application/feed+json\"` in metadata\n\n\n- Line 146: Already has explicit `<link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/feed+json\" title=\"Pelangi Blog\" href=\"/feed.json\" />`\n\nSo the metadata approach is already generating the feed links via Next.js, but I need to verify whether the acceptance criteria requires the explicit `<link>` tags in addition to or instead of the metadata configuration.\n\nLooking at what's needed: the RSS feed link tag is missing from the explicit `<head>` tags, and I still need to create the actual `/feed.json` route handler. Let me check the blog page structure to understand what data I'm working with.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3578,"cache_read_input_tokens":31277,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3578},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48cd3948-144c-45c7-ae83-7eda8bdfa883","uuid":"c4eb3576-c33e-49f4-a51d-e96a1014341e"}
