{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012zbzzfshk7NmR6nQEkQfcj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\texport interface BlogPost {\n2\t  slug: string;\n3\t  title: string;\n4\t  excerpt: string;\n5\t  content: string; // HTML string\n6\t  date: string; // YYYY-MM-DD\n7\t  category: string;\n8\t  author: string;\n9\t  readTime: string;\n10\t  readingTimeMinutes: number;\n11\t  tags: string[];\n12\t  featuredImage: string;\n13\t}\n14\t\n15\t/** Compute reading time from HTML content (200 wpm, minimum 1 min). */\n16\tfunction computeReadingTime(html: string): number {\n17\t  const text = html.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, \" \").replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim();\n18\t  const wordCount = text.split(\" \").filter(Boolean).length;\n19\t  return Math.max(1, Math.ceil(wordCount / 200));\n20\t}\n21\t\n22\t/** Converts a category label to a URL-safe slug. e.g. \"Food & Drink\" → \"food-drink\" */\n23\texport function categoryToSlug(category: string): string {\n24\t  return category\n25\t    .toLowerCase()\n26\t    .replace(/[^a-z0-9\\s]/g, \"\")\n27\t    .trim()\n28\t    .replace(/\\s+/g, \"-\");\n29\t}\n30\t\n31\t/** Converts a category slug back to a display label, or returns null if not found. */\n32\texport function slugToCategory(slug: string): string | null {\n33\t  const found = blogPosts.find((p) => categoryToSlug(p.category) === slug);\n34\t  return found ? found.category : null;\n35\t}\n36\t\n37\t/** All unique categories in the blog. */\n38\texport function getUniqueCategories(): string[] {\n39\t  return [...new Set(blogPosts.map((p) => p.category))];\n40\t}\n41\t\n42\tconst rawPosts: Omit<BlogPost, \"readingTimeMinutes\">[] = [\n43\t  {\n44\t    slug: \"ultimate-jb-food-guide-backpackers\",\n45\t    title: \"The Ultimate Johor Bahru Food Guide for Backpackers (2026)\",\n46\t    excerpt:\n47\t      \"From RM5 hawker meals to legendary seafood spots — everything a budget traveller needs to eat their way through JB like a local.\",\n48\t    date: \"2026-02-20\",\n49\t    category: \"Food & Drink\",\n50\t    author: \"Pelangi Team\","}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48cd3948-144c-45c7-ae83-7eda8bdfa883","uuid":"2afbd996-a6a5-4b93-a3ed-56c6f500177e","timestamp":"2026-04-14T05:15:56.535Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts","content":"export interface BlogPost {\n  slug: string;\n  title: string;\n  excerpt: string;\n  content: string; // HTML string\n  date: string; // YYYY-MM-DD\n  category: string;\n  author: string;\n  readTime: string;\n  readingTimeMinutes: number;\n  tags: string[];\n  featuredImage: string;\n}\n\n/** Compute reading time from HTML content (200 wpm, minimum 1 min). */\nfunction computeReadingTime(html: string): number {\n  const text = html.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, \" \").replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim();\n  const wordCount = text.split(\" \").filter(Boolean).length;\n  return Math.max(1, Math.ceil(wordCount / 200));\n}\n\n/** Converts a category label to a URL-safe slug. e.g. \"Food & Drink\" → \"food-drink\" */\nexport function categoryToSlug(category: string): string {\n  return category\n    .toLowerCase()\n    .replace(/[^a-z0-9\\s]/g, \"\")\n    .trim()\n    .replace(/\\s+/g, \"-\");\n}\n\n/** Converts a category slug back to a display label, or returns null if not found. */\nexport function slugToCategory(slug: string): string | null {\n  const found = blogPosts.find((p) => categoryToSlug(p.category) === slug);\n  return found ? found.category : null;\n}\n\n/** All unique categories in the blog. */\nexport function getUniqueCategories(): string[] {\n  return [...new Set(blogPosts.map((p) => p.category))];\n}\n\nconst rawPosts: Omit<BlogPost, \"readingTimeMinutes\">[] = [\n  {\n    slug: \"ultimate-jb-food-guide-backpackers\",\n    title: \"The Ultimate Johor Bahru Food Guide for Backpackers (2026)\",\n    excerpt:\n      \"From RM5 hawker meals to legendary seafood spots — everything a budget traveller needs to eat their way through JB like a local.\",\n    date: \"2026-02-20\",\n    category: \"Food & Drink\",\n    author: \"Pelangi Team\",","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":843}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_018bKqESPM2XVorX6oEuT7hv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the structure. Let me assess what needs to be done:\n\n1. **layout.tsx**: Looking at it again, lines 59-61 have `alternates.types` with both RSS and JSON Feed URLs in the metadata object. Next.js converts this to `<link rel=\"alternate\">` tags. But also line 146 has an explicit `<link>` tag for JSON Feed only. The AC says to add `<link rel='alternate' type='application/rss+xml' href='/feed.xml' />` to the metadata. \n\n   Wait, re-reading the AC: \"Add `<link rel='alternate' type='application/rss+xml' href='/feed.xml' />` and `<link rel='alternate' type='application/feed+json' href='/feed.json' />` to `site/src/app/layout.tsx` metadata\"\n   \n   The metadata already has both feeds covered through the `alternates.types` API, which Next.js will render as the proper link tags. There's an explicit JSON Feed link in the head at line 146, so I need to check if an explicit RSS link tag is also needed or if the metadata approach is sufficient for the acceptance criteria.\n\nLooking at what's actually missing: the explicit RSS `<link>` tag in the head. The feed.json route exists but returns all posts instead of limiting to 10 as required. And there's no test file for the feed route yet.\n\nSo I'll add the RSS link tag to the layout, slice the posts array to 10 in the feed route, and create a test file to verify the JSON Feed structure.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":773,"cache_read_input_tokens":39365,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":773},"output_tokens":33,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48cd3948-144c-45c7-ae83-7eda8bdfa883","uuid":"a25914f2-154f-420