{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01T537rmTp6gimFSkrxq3wmB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AyqbqaRt1A6hsJR1CJtmKb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\" && python -c \"\nprogress = open('progress.txt', encoding='utf-8').read()\nentry = '''\n\n## Iteration N - Story: US-265 - RSS auto-discovery link tag and JSON Feed 1.1\n\n### What was implemented\n- layout.tsx already had both RSS and JSON Feed link tags (RSS at line 146, JSON Feed at line 148) — verified AC1 already satisfied\n- feed.json/route.ts already limited to 10 posts with .slice(0, 10) — AC2 already satisfied\n- Created site/src/app/feed.json/route.test.ts with 5 tests: version, item count, required fields, content-type, sort order\n- Created site/vitest.config.ts with @/ path alias resolution for vitest\n\n### Patterns discovered\n- vitest needs a vitest.config.ts with resolve.alias for @/* -> ./src/* when running outside Next.js build\n- Both layout.tsx link tags and alternates.types metadata exist (Next.js renders alternates.types as <link> tags automatically)\n\n### Gotchas\n- The route and layout were already updated by a prior SPIRAL iteration; only the test file was missing\n- Must create vitest.config.ts in site/ to resolve @/ alias, otherwise vitest cannot find @/data/blog/posts\n'''\nwith open('progress.txt', 'a', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    f.write(entry)\nprint('Done')\n\"","description":"Append learnings to progress.txt"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":202,"cache_read_input_tokens":54664,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":202},"output_tokens":57,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48cd3948-144